Z||000010||Loki||02-22-2001||09:52 AM||||The pic is not accurate, yes the wing has some sag to it but near as bad as the pic makes it out to be...And so far the only mechanical problems it has are, needs new front rotors and pads, and some suspension work (struts/shocks and ball joints)So im going to save my lunch money and go buck wild on this one.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Phil||02-22-2001||10:56 AM||||There is a way to correct a sagging wing. Take the stands off- turn the wing upside down and support it at the ends. Lay some bags of lead shot in the middle to make the wing straight. Drill two holes into the wing where the stands mount. Fill the wing with that insulating expanding foam. Let the foam fully cure(24 hrs. at least). Ta-Da||||reg||1
